  m_text: "The Sun\u2019s activity follows an approximately 11-year cycle known as
    the solar cycle. During this cycle, the number of sunspots increases to a peak
    known as solar maximum, then decreases to a minimum. This cycle influences solar
    flares, coronal mass ejections, and variations in solar radiation. Tracking the
    solar cycle helps scientists predict space weather events that can affect Earth\u2019s
    technological systems."
